Interactive USD edits of the color space of a ParticleField3DGaussianSplat, with the usd procedural cache_id and with the render delegate

see #2845

A ParticleField3DGaussianSplat gets a colorSpace:name (UsdColorSpaceAPI), then primvars:arnold:gs_input_color_space
overriding it, which is removed, then a colorSpace metadata on its spherical harmonics coefficients, stronger than the
colorSpace:name. The splat is mid grey, which is about 0.21 when decoded as sRGB (Arnold's default) and 0.5 in a linear
color space. See test_2845.1 for Houdini's splats.
The scenario runs with the "usd" procedural reading the stage through its cache_id in an interactive render session,
and with the HdArnoldRendererPlugin render delegate driven like a Hydra host, see
testsuite/common/interactive_usd_test.h. Each render is checked in test.cpp, and the last procedural render is
compared against the reference image. UsdImaging only gives the USD color space to Hydra 2, so the Hydra 1 renders
report it as a known issue.

author: sebastien.blaineau.ortega@autodesk.com

PARAMS: {'program_env': 'interactive_usd'}
